{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - System API - Okta API Token Created",
	"Description": "An Okta API token was created. An API token is a long-lived credential that bypasses interactive sign-in and MFA entirely, so creating one is a standard way to keep access to an org after the initial compromise.\n\nEvent type: system.api_token.create\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/persistence_attempt_to_create_okta_api_token/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/persistence_attempt_to_create_okta_api_token.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
